# Copy to .env only if you need it. Normally you do NOT -- services/api.js derives
# the API address from the Metro bundler's host, which is your Mac's LAN address.
#
# Set this when:
#   - you run `npx expo start --tunnel` (hostUri becomes an exp.direct domain)
#   - you point the app at a deployed server
#
# EXPO_PUBLIC_ is not a convention, it is a requirement: Expo only inlines variables
# with that prefix into the client bundle. And that means anything here IS public --
# never put a secret in this file.

# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://192.168.1.42:8080/api
